Subject: [PATCH 02488/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE
 skeptic-proofing; GATED on exp4370 llm_heuristic_beats_linear==true) --
 CONTAMINATION/LEAKAGE SKEPTIC-PROOF of the A1 LLM-generated-heuristic win. IF
 exp4370 shows the stronger function class beats the deployed linear heuristic
 on held-out actions, the operator (twice-burned on over-claims) will ask: is
 the win from a genuinely-stronger heuristic, or from (a) public-ARC-layout
 MEMORIZATION (the LLM saw these games in pretraining), (b) hidden
 game-specific SHORTCUTS, or (c) single-held-out-split OVERFIT? This
 DIAGNOSTIC (no new heuristic synthesis, no env-grade gate) re-tests the A1
 winning heuristics three ways: (1) FRESH-GAME generalization -- run them on
 games NOT in the A1 selection set + with the LEAST likely pretraining
 overlap; (2) a DYNAMIC leakage trace (instrument the heuristic at eval to
 confirm it touches ONLY observable grid features, never the goal predicate /
 answer cells); (3) a SECOND held-out split (different leave-out) to rule out
 single-split overfit. Emit win_is_contamination_free BARE bool := (the A1
 advantage survives a fresh-game/second-split re-test with the dynamic leakage
 trace clean, CI95 of the held-out action delta excludes 0).
 verifier_is_oracle=false. A pass = the efficiency-moat deepening is GENUINE
 (the headline graduates); a fail = the A1 win is contamination-confounded and
 is QUARANTINED + the residual logged as a missing-verifier gap. NO TRM
 training; CPU-offline.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4370-llm-generated-action-cost-heuristics.llm_heuristic_beats_linear (actual=False == expected=True)

